Commit:     Alex Ong <alex@entire.io>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 20 16:29:21 2026 +1000

    fix(trail): gate the non-interactive etag refetch on the actual branch, warn on failure

    Review found the best-effort etag refetch in the non-interactive --body
    path was keyed on bodyETag=="" rather than on which branch actually ran,
    so it could also fire mid-interactive-session on a blank baseline and
    pair a freshly-fetched etag with content the user never saw. Gate it on
    !noFlags instead, and warn (rather than silently degrade) when the
    refetch itself fails, mirroring the interactive path's existing warning.

    Also: resolveTrailUpdateBody now keeps a real etag even when the
    description is legitimately empty (it describes the document, not the
    text), a doc comment overclaiming write-etag-chaining is fixed, and
    sendTrailBody's three-mode dispatch collapses two identical switch arms
    into one if/else.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0199BaBLje6ytF8kKGUkGocS
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M0EXR9BAEFGQ216WSWMGT3C3
